# Every text here derives more than one way, on purpose.
#
# `sum` is left- and right-associative at once, so "1+2+3" is two
# different trees that mean two different things. lexic REFUSES that
# rather than picking: open the floor to see the verdict, derivations
# to see both, and the resolver chip to choose.
root ::= sum
sum ::= sum "+" sum | num
num ::= [0-9]+
